# Line endings.
#
# Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true, which stores LF in the index but
# checks out CRLF. That produces a "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning on
# every file, and one real hazard: packages/web/docker-entrypoint.sh would be
# checked out with CRLF, and `#!/bin/sh\r` is not a valid interpreter inside a
# Linux container. The failure is obscure - the script appears correct and the
# container exits immediately.
#
# The repository is Prettier-formatted with LF throughout, so normalise on both
# sides and let the attribute win over autocrlf.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the files where CRLF would actually break something, so the
# intent survives someone relaxing the wildcard above.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch these, and never try to diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
